<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || this.get(i) == null) && (\old(this.get(i)) == null || \old(this.get(i)) == this.get(i));</code>

However, since the elements at indices before the specified index should remain unchanged, we can simplify the assert statement to:

<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This ensures that for every valid index before the specified index, the element at that position remains unchanged.
